UID:10021834-1786037400-1786041000@events.ubc.ca
SUMMARY:Zippered Wood: Rethinking How We Build
DESCRIPTION:What happens when computational design intersects with construction-grade lumber and contemporary digital workflows?  \nDigital ideas leave the screen and become full-scale physical structures. Discover how researchers are using accessible tools to rethink what’s possible with wood.  \nJoin us on August 6th from 5:30-6:30 PM in IKB 301 for an EML Workshop featuring researchers from SALA’s HiLo Lab presenting Zippered Wood\, an ongoing research project exploring how computational design\, conventional construction methods\, and accessible fabrication tools can be combined to create sophisticated approaches to timber design and fabrication.  \nThrough built projects\, prototypes\, and demonstrations\, the team will trace the project’s evolution from digital models to full-scale physical assemblies while exploring how contemporary digital workflows can expand the possibilities of architectural design. \n🔗 RSVP through the link: https://ubc.ca1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_6xwMdVnHHFgsNj8  
URL:https://events.ubc.ca/event/zippered-wood-rethinking-how-we-build/
LOCATION:Irving K. Barber Learning Centre\, 1961 East Mall\, Vancouver\, British Columbia\, V6T1Z1\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Audience - All,Audience – All Students,Audience – Alumni,Audience – Community
ORGANIZER;CN="UBC Emerging Media Lab":MAILTO:emergingmedia.lab@ubc.ca
END:VEVENT
